WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.780
Hi, I'm Erik Voss, and we've been getting
new updates about the upcoming Venom

00:00:03.780 --> 00:00:07.350
movie, with spider-man's best villain
getting his own solo film produced by

00:00:07.350 --> 00:00:09.510
Sony.
Tom Hardy will be playing Venom slash

00:00:09.510 --> 00:00:13.860
Eddie Brock, and freaking Carnage is going
to be playing the villain. So venom and

00:00:13.860 --> 00:00:18.690
Carnage together in a movie is a huge
deal, and this is probably why Sony

00:00:18.690 --> 00:00:21.600
announced that this movie will
definitely be rated R. And this R

00:00:21.600 --> 00:00:25.109
rating is interesting, because it brings
into question how Venom and Carnage

00:00:25.109 --> 00:00:29.279
could ever fit into the overall
cinematic universe of Marvel characters,

00:00:29.279 --> 00:00:32.579
with the MCU known as pretty
family-friendly versions of these

00:00:32.579 --> 00:00:35.520
superheroes and villains.
Now even though Sony and Marvel Studios

00:00:35.520 --> 00:00:39.629
are partnering to allow spider-man as a
character to cross over into the MCU, and

00:00:39.629 --> 00:00:42.960
with movies like Spider-man: Homecoming,
Marvel head, Kevin Feige, has made it

00:00:42.960 --> 00:00:46.710
clear that this will not be the case for
the Venom movie. So it sounds like Venom

00:00:46.710 --> 00:00:50.370
and Carnage will be in their own
separate movie universe, where maybe

00:00:50.370 --> 00:00:55.590
spider-man might appear, according to Amy
Pascal of Sony, but Venom won't appear in

00:00:55.590 --> 00:01:00.480
scenes with or even really reference MCU
characters like Iron Man, Captain

00:01:00.480 --> 00:01:03.809
America, Thor or Hulk. Now at first this
seems like kind of a bummer, because

00:01:03.809 --> 00:01:06.570
these guys have a lot of fun
interactions with all these other Marvel

00:01:06.570 --> 00:01:09.930
characters in the comics, but I think
this could ultimately be a good thing.

00:01:09.930 --> 00:01:14.820
Why? Because Venom needs to have an R
rating. He is a violent, monstrous killer,

00:01:14.820 --> 00:01:19.439
Carnage even more so, and I just don't
see Marvel Studios, in the direction that

00:01:19.439 --> 00:01:23.460
it's currently going, being willing to
adapt Venom and Carnage to screen in

00:01:23.460 --> 00:01:27.689
their true terrifying forms. So let's
talk about Venom and Carnage, why they're

00:01:27.689 --> 00:01:31.740
such great villains, and why keeping them
out of the Marvel side of the Cinematic

00:01:31.740 --> 00:01:35.009
Universe might be the best thing for
them. And potential spoiler warning, in

00:01:35.009 --> 00:01:38.610
case any of my speculation with stuff
from the comics ends up being in the

00:01:38.610 --> 00:01:41.880
movie. So let's start with a little
background on Venom. Venom comes from an

00:01:41.880 --> 00:01:46.320
alien race of symbiotes who, in the comics,
he attaches himself to Spider-man when

00:01:46.320 --> 00:01:49.079
he was in Battle World, which is a big
melee with a ton of different

00:01:49.079 --> 00:01:53.070
superheroes and villains. So Peter's suit
was damaged and the symbiote covered his

00:01:53.070 --> 00:01:57.930
body, giving him this new awesome black
suit with a white logo. It also had a

00:01:57.930 --> 00:02:01.950
shape-shifting ability, allowing him to
mimic wearing street clothes, and gave

00:02:01.950 --> 00:02:05.610
him an unlimited and stronger supply of
webbing. But then Peter learned that the

00:02:05.610 --> 00:02:09.239
symbiote was really a parasite that
eventually drains all the adrenaline

00:02:09.239 --> 00:02:12.110
from its host, so he detached it using
the

00:02:12.110 --> 00:02:15.710
sonic waves from the bells in a church
bell tower. And then the symbiote

00:02:15.710 --> 00:02:19.460
sought out another person who hated
Peter Parker, ex-journalist Eddie Brock,

00:02:19.460 --> 00:02:23.120
who's career Peter ended. And it merged
with Eddie Brock, creating Venom. Now

00:02:23.120 --> 00:02:26.180
some of this backstory was adapted for
the version of Venom that we saw in

00:02:26.180 --> 00:02:29.690
Spider-man 3 with Topher Grace, and
unfortunately that movie didn't really

00:02:29.690 --> 00:02:33.050
do nearly enough with the character.
Spider-man 3 really just mostly stuck

00:02:33.050 --> 00:02:36.980
with Peter's relationship with a symbiote,
which turned him into a kind of pervy

00:02:36.980 --> 00:02:41.450
dancer, with the Eddie Brock / Venom
subplots getting lost in Peter's conflicts

00:02:41.450 --> 00:02:44.750
with Harry Osborn and Sandman. And as
much as I love to watch James Franco

00:02:44.750 --> 00:02:47.540
eating pie, I'd rather see Venom do some
messed-up shit.

00:02:47.540 --> 00:02:52.040
And this is why I'm excited about this
R-rated Venom movie. Venom is savage, a

00:02:52.040 --> 00:02:55.280
big part of its popularity is that he's
very much a bizarro version of

00:02:55.280 --> 00:02:58.700
Spider-man (and sorry to mix in a DC
reference in there.) Like Peter Parker is

00:02:58.700 --> 00:03:03.620
super friendly, and neighborhoody! He's a
kid, he cracks jokes, but Venom is a total

00:03:03.620 --> 00:03:07.070
monster. Since he previously bonded with
Spider-man as a symbiote, all later

00:03:07.070 --> 00:03:10.880
versions of Venom have Spider-man's powers, too.
He's a lot stronger, and he's a

00:03:10.880 --> 00:03:13.700
shapeshifter,
and he's invisible to Spider-man's spidey

00:03:13.700 --> 00:03:17.150
sense, making him a serious threat. In
fact in the comics, he's considered by

00:03:17.150 --> 00:03:20.150
Shield to be one of the biggest dangers
to all of humanity,

00:03:20.150 --> 00:03:24.380
up there with Magneto and Dr. Doom. And
already, you just can't do that character

00:03:24.380 --> 00:03:29.209
justice with a PG-13 MCU type movie that
you would take little kids to go see.

00:03:29.209 --> 00:03:32.480
Unless you want them to grow up to be
cool. And the director currently attached

00:03:32.480 --> 00:03:36.739
to Venom is Ruben Fleischer, who directed
Zombieland, and I really hope that he

00:03:36.739 --> 00:03:40.580
brings that same dark, violent sense of
humor to this movie, too. Now I actually

00:03:40.580 --> 00:03:45.140
kind of like Sam Raimi's design of the
symbiote in Spider-man 3, but I think

00:03:45.140 --> 00:03:48.739
Fleischer can build on that to make
Venom even more monstrous and

00:03:48.739 --> 00:03:51.590
stomach-turning. I'm just going to give
you a few examples of some of the

00:03:51.590 --> 00:03:55.580
sickening stuff that Venom has done in
various versions of the comics. 1. Later

00:03:55.580 --> 00:04:00.620
host of Venom, Mac Gargan formerly the
Scorpion, isn't as good as Eddie Brock is

00:04:00.620 --> 00:04:05.060
at controlling the symbiote, so he gives
into some of the more animalistic urges,

00:04:05.060 --> 00:04:09.680
specifically cannibalism. Yes,
Venom freaking eats people. And that same

00:04:09.680 --> 00:04:15.079
version of Venom also gets in a fight
with Bullseye, who throws a small dog into

00:04:15.079 --> 00:04:18.799
Venom's eye, and Venom continues fighting
with the dog sticking out of his eye,

00:04:18.799 --> 00:04:22.650
until later he pops it out and chucks it.
Now another version of Venom detaches

00:04:22.650 --> 00:04:26.220
from a host who's a mobster's son, Angelo
Fortunato.

00:04:26.220 --> 00:04:29.699
In the middle of a jump between
buildings, he lets the guy fall to his

00:04:29.699 --> 00:04:34.350
death. Then there's a really bad version
of the Venom comics from the mid-2000s,

00:04:34.350 --> 00:04:38.430
where Venom fights with the Thing from
the Fantastic Four, and he kills him by

00:04:38.430 --> 00:04:42.509
sticking his long tongue down his throat.
And then there's another alternate

00:04:42.509 --> 00:04:46.229
series of Marvel comics called What If,
where the Battle World arc that I

00:04:46.229 --> 00:04:50.400
mentioned earlier goes a different way,
and Spider-man is on a planet with his

00:04:50.400 --> 00:04:54.630
symbiote black suit, but then he gets
hit with a sonic blast and the symbiote

00:04:54.630 --> 00:04:58.919
detaches from Peter Parker's skeleton.
That's right, Peter Parker had been dead

00:04:58.919 --> 00:05:02.550
for years and the symbiote form of Venom
was just Weekend at Bernie-ing his

00:05:02.550 --> 00:05:06.780
corpse all this time! But really, it's not
just this insane, creative violence that

00:05:06.780 --> 00:05:10.979
makes Venom a more adult character, and
yeah it isn't profanity either... it's the

00:05:10.979 --> 00:05:14.610
sex. I'm kidding guys, I really don't want
to see Venom have sex.

00:05:14.610 --> 00:05:17.610
I really shouldn't've brought up that
example... with the Thing. Really, it's the

00:05:17.610 --> 00:05:21.990
deeper psychological component of Venom
as a character. Now as a symbiote bonded

00:05:21.990 --> 00:05:25.800
with a host, there's kind of a split
personality competing for control of

00:05:25.800 --> 00:05:30.900
Eddie Brock's mind. It's a toxic balance
of the two organisms' hatred feeding and

00:05:30.900 --> 00:05:34.620
enabling each other. And that was another
element that the Spider-man 3 Venom just

00:05:34.620 --> 00:05:37.860
didn't have enough time to go into.
And really, I don't know how far the MCU

00:05:37.860 --> 00:05:42.060
would be willing to explore that kind of
psychological disorder. Like Iron Man 3

00:05:42.060 --> 00:05:45.780
kind of touched on Tony Stark's PTSD
from the Battle of New York, and

00:05:45.780 --> 00:05:49.349
I guess Doctor Strange looked at
Stephen's depression after his car accident,

00:05:49.349 --> 00:05:52.860
but the competing voices in Eddie
Brock's head are something that he has

00:05:52.860 --> 00:05:56.460
to deal with in a very physical way, and
that's a conflict that's going to take a

00:05:56.460 --> 00:06:01.110
lot of maturity and patience to convey
on screen. For example, look at Logan.

00:06:01.110 --> 00:06:04.620
Director James Mangold said that the R
rating for that movie wasn't just so he

00:06:04.620 --> 00:06:07.889
could show Wolverine clawing through skulls,
even though that was very cool and I'm

00:06:07.889 --> 00:06:11.580
glad I got to see it. Mangold said that
he wanted to explore characters and

00:06:11.580 --> 00:06:15.240
relationships in a way that didn't also
have to please audiences with shorter

00:06:15.240 --> 00:06:19.110
attention spans. So that's why huge
sections of Logan simply focused on the

00:06:19.110 --> 00:06:23.340
mental, emotional, and physical toll that
superpowers have taken on Logan and

00:06:23.340 --> 00:06:27.389
Charles. They're people, not toys. They get
sick, they aren't always likable, and

00:06:27.389 --> 00:06:30.360
spoiler alert - seriously, stop watching if
you haven't seen Logan -

00:06:30.360 --> 00:06:34.139
they kiss! Just kidding, they die. Now I
don't always need my superhero

00:06:34.139 --> 00:06:37.889
movies to go that deep into a
character's psychological trauma. Like Thor

00:06:37.889 --> 00:06:41.819
Ragnarok looks like ridiculous fun, and I
would be kind of bummed if it ever got

00:06:41.819 --> 00:06:45.840
this serious, but in Venom's case, yeah, I
really think it needs to be more

00:06:45.840 --> 00:06:49.710
emotionally complex. And I really think
Tom Hardy is perfect for that kind of

00:06:49.710 --> 00:06:53.430
raw, physical role. He's a serious actor
who puts his whole body into a

00:06:53.430 --> 00:06:56.370
performance. I just hope that for this
superhero villain he'll pick a

00:06:56.370 --> 00:06:59.580
different voice. Your spidey sense won't
save you now,

00:06:59.580 --> 00:07:04.289
Parker. But let's move on to Carnage, the
villain of this movie. Yeah, that's right,

00:07:04.289 --> 00:07:08.099
Carnage is so awful that even Venom sees
him as a threat that needs to be

00:07:08.099 --> 00:07:11.900
stopped. So a little background on
Carnage in the comics. So Carnage is the

00:07:11.900 --> 00:07:17.039
asexual offspring of Venom's symbiote. And
it attaches to Cletus Kasady,

00:07:17.039 --> 00:07:21.090
who's a serial killer whom Eddie Brock
shares a prison cell with. And Kasady is

00:07:21.090 --> 00:07:26.069
already totally evil. As a kid, he
tortured his family dog with an electric

00:07:26.069 --> 00:07:29.969
drill, and he killed his grandmother by
pushing her down a flight of stairs. He

00:07:29.969 --> 00:07:33.360
also burned down the boys home that he
was forced to live in. So when Kasady

00:07:33.360 --> 00:07:37.349
becomes Carnage he just goes on
straight-up killing sprees, just to get

00:07:37.349 --> 00:07:40.589
Spider-man's attention, and really,
because he just feels like it. He murders

00:07:40.589 --> 00:07:45.210
one of Peter Parker's classmates, and he
can shape-shift his arms into cutting

00:07:45.210 --> 00:07:50.129
weapons, slicing and impaling the bodies
of innocent bystanders on the street and

00:07:50.129 --> 00:07:54.750
in diners. He attacks a little kid and a
baby in a bathtub, and he kills people

00:07:54.750 --> 00:07:59.039
through computer screens, and he
constantly fantasizes about mutilating

00:07:59.039 --> 00:08:04.529
Peter Parker. So really, as intense as
Venom is, Carnage is way more extreme, and

00:08:04.529 --> 00:08:07.649
again, there's just no way this would
work in anything less than an R

00:08:07.649 --> 00:08:12.419
rating. So if Sony really plans to go in
this direction with a darker, more adult

00:08:12.419 --> 00:08:16.560
superhero movie universe separate from
the family-friendly MCU, they're really

00:08:16.560 --> 00:08:20.069
right to set the tone early with this
Venom movie. It really is the best way to

00:08:20.069 --> 00:08:23.849
be true to what fans love from the
comics. Do you think a movie version of

00:08:23.849 --> 00:08:27.659
Venom that will never cross paths with
Iron Man or Captain America or Hulk or

00:08:27.659 --> 00:08:31.860
for that matter, Daredevil or Punisher, is
worth its own movie universe if that

00:08:31.860 --> 00:08:35.940
universe gets to be dark, adult and
violent? And do you think Venom should

00:08:35.940 --> 00:08:40.529
use this R rating for more extreme
violence? Or to explore that kind of

00:08:40.529 --> 00:08:43.769
psychological trauma stuff on a level
that younger audiences just might not

00:08:43.769 --> 00:08:47.089
appreciate? Let me know what you think in
the comments down below and share this

